# recorder: the DB8E shows the transport mode as a word (issue #22, Group C).
#
# recorder.md "Display": "the display will show **Recording**, **Playback** or
# **Bypass** whenever you change the recording mode." STOP maps to "Bypass" —
# the manual's own name for idle: "The circuit starts in idle / stopped mode
# and `L1.3` is lit. In that mode the input is bypassed to the output."
#
# Those three words never appear in the patch, so they are not in the text
# table the parser builds. They are interned at load through
# Circuit::internTexts and sent as the Text layout — the load-time seam for
# circuit-provided strings (docs/adr/0003-db8e-custom-display-layouts.md).
#
# The circuit has no scalar `output` jack, so there is no automatic title to
# derive (issue #19's "no `output` jack -> no header at all, just the value")
# and the header is empty unless the patch sets one.
#
# Transport timing mirrors recorder/buttons-and-leds.gold.
patch <<<
[db8e]

[recorder]
    recordbutton = I1
    playbutton   = I2
    stopbutton   = I3
    cvin         = I4
    cvout        = O1
>>>
# Merely loading the patch leaves the screen dark, even though the circuit is
# already in its idle/bypass mode: the screen wakes on a mode CHANGE.
@0 set I4 0.50
@0 expectdisplay D1 off
# record button -> RECORD
@1 set I1 1
@1 set I4 0.51
@1 expectdisplay D1 text "Recording"
@1 expectdisplay D1 header ""
@2 set I1 0
@2 set I4 0.52
# Still recording, nothing changed: the screen holds the same word.
@2 expectdisplay D1 text "Recording"
@3 set I4 0.53
# stop button -> idle, which is "Bypass"
@4 set I3 1
@4 set I4 0.53
@4 expectdisplay D1 text "Bypass"
# play button -> PLAY
@5 set I3 0
@5 set I2 1
@5 expectdisplay D1 text "Playback"
@6 set I2 0
@6 expectdisplay D1 text "Playback"
@7 expectdisplay D1 text "Playback"
# The tape runs out. With the buttons (not `mode`) that auto-stops back to
# idle, which is a mode change like any other -> "Bypass" again. The screen
# follows the mode that drove the tick's OUTPUT, so it changes in lockstep
# with the stop LED rather than a tick ahead of it.
@8 set I4 0.77
@8 expect O1 0.77 tol 1e-5
@8 expectdisplay D1 text "Bypass"
@9 expectdisplay D1 text "Bypass"
